<!--
    kuna `option returndup` value `auto` (the default), P8 goto-quality: in
    a function the per-function detector (p3_dataflow/kuna_unoptimized.rs)
    calls unoptimized, the return statements read from the raw block graph
    (p8_structure/kuna_o0returns.rs) decide which shared epilogues are split.

    gcc 11 -O0 (-fno-pic -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none) of
        extern void use(int);
        int guard(int c) { if (!c) return 0; use(1); return 0; }
        int wrapped(int c) { if (c) { use(2); } return 3; }
        void vguard(int c) { if (c) return; use(4); }
        int pick(int c, int a, int b) { if (c) return a; return b; }
    guard's first return is its own "mov eax,0; jmp" block, wrapped's epilogue
    sets eax itself, vguard's return is a nop the test jumps to, and pick's two
    returns each load eax before the epilogue.

    Pass 1 (default auto): guard keeps its guard clause (#1, #2), wrapped
    keeps one return (#3), vguard keeps its bare return (#4) and pick returns
    each parameter (#5). Pass 2 (option returndup on, the old default): guard
    and vguard are wrapped under the size rule (#6, #7) and pick merges its
    returns into one variable (#8).
-->
